PART 4: THE COMPLETE DATA FLOW PATTERN

================================================================================

Step 1: Parent Stores Data
import { useState } from 'react';
import Child from './Child';

export default function Parent() {

  const [count, setCount] =
    useState(0);

  return (
    <div>

      <h1>
        Parent Component
      </h1>

      <p>
        Count: {count}
      </p>

      <Child count={count} />

    </div>
  );
}

Explanation
Code                    | Purpose
------------------------|----------------------------------------
useState(0)             | Creates count state
count                   | Current state value
setCount                | State update function
Parent                  | Owns the state
count={count}           | Passes count to Child


Flow:

PARENT STATE
count = 0
    ↓
<Child count={count} />
    ↓
CHILD RECEIVES count


================================================================================

Step 2: Child Receives Data

================================================================================

export default function Child(props) {

  return (
    <div>

      <h1>
        Child Component
      </h1>

      <p>
        Received count: {props.count}
      </p>

    </div>
  );
}

Explanation
Code             | Purpose
-----------------|--------------------------------
props            | Contains values from parent
props.count      | Reads count supplied by parent


The child displays the value but doesn't own the parent's count state.

================================================================================

Step 3: Parent Passes an Update Function

================================================================================

import { useState } from 'react';
import Child from './Child';

export default function Parent() {

  const [count, setCount] =
    useState(0);

  const incrementCount = () => {
    setCount(count + 1);
  };

  return (
    <div>

      <h1>
        Parent Component
      </h1>

      <p>
        Count: {count}
      </p>

      <Child
        count={count}
        onIncrement={incrementCount}
      />

    </div>
  );
}

Explanation
Code                         | Purpose
-----------------------------|---------------------------------------
incrementCount()             | Parent-owned update logic
setCount(count + 1)          | Updates parent's state
count={count}                | Passes current data
onIncrement={incrementCount} | Passes callback function


================================================================================

Step 4: Child Calls the Parent Function

================================================================================

export default function Child(props) {

  return (
    <div>

      <h1>
        Child Component
      </h1>

      <p>
        Count: {props.count}
      </p>

      <button
        onClick={props.onIncrement}
      >
        Increment
      </button>

    </div>
  );
}

Flow
USER CLICKS
     ↓
props.onIncrement()
     ↓
PARENT'S incrementCount()
     ↓
setCount(...)
     ↓
PARENT STATE CHANGES
     ↓
PARENT RE-RENDERS
     ↓
NEW count PROP
     ↓
CHILD RE-RENDERS


================================================================================

COMPLETE ONE-WAY DATA FLOW CYCLE

================================================================================

Step | Flow
-----|-------------------------------------------------------
1    | Parent state starts with count = 0
2    | Parent passes count={0} to Child
3    | Child displays Count: 0
4    | User clicks Child's button
5    | Child calls onIncrement()
6    | Parent's incrementCount() executes
7    | Parent updates count to 1
8    | Parent renders Child with count={1}
9    | Child receives the new count prop
10   | Child displays Count: 1

Easy Memory
STATE
  ↓
PROPS
  ↓
CHILD
  ↓
EVENT
  ↓
CALLBACK
  ↓
PARENT STATE UPDATE
  ↓
NEW PROPS
  ↓
UPDATED UI


