PART 6: WHY ONE-WAY DATA FLOW MATTERS

================================================================================

Benefit 1: Predictability

You can trace:

Question               | Answer
-----------------------|--------------------------------
Where data comes from? | Parent state/props
Where data goes?       | Child components
Who owns the state?    | State-owning component
How is it updated?     | State owner's update function
How child requests it? | Callback prop


================================================================================

Benefit 2: Easier Debugging

================================================================================

If a child displays unexpected data:

CHECK CHILD PROPS
      ↓
CHECK PARENT DATA/STATE
      ↓
CHECK UPDATE CALLBACK
      ↓
CHECK STATE UPDATE


The directional flow makes the source of data easier to trace.

================================================================================

Benefit 3: Clearer Dependencies

================================================================================

Preferred flow:

Parent
  ↓
Child
  ↓
Grandchild


Updates are requested through callbacks rather than children directly mutating parent-owned state.

This gives data and state clear ownership.

================================================================================

Benefit 4: Easier Testing

================================================================================

A child receiving props can be tested conceptually as:

GIVEN PROPS
    ↓
RENDER COMPONENT
    ↓
VERIFY OUTPUT


Callback behavior:

USER ACTION
    ↓
CALLBACK INVOKED
    ↓
VERIFY EXPECTED VALUE


