PART 7: COMMON MISTAKES

================================================================================

Mistake 1: Trying to Modify Props

Wrong:

function Child(props) {

  props.count = 5;

  return (
    <h1>
      {props.count}
    </h1>
  );
}


Correct:

function Child(props) {

  return (
    <h1>
      {props.count}
    </h1>
  );
}

Rule
PROPS = READ-ONLY INPUT


================================================================================

Mistake 2: Trying to Update Parent Data Directly

================================================================================

Wrong

Parent:

function Parent() {

  const [count, setCount] =
    useState(0);

  return (
    <Child count={count} />
  );
}


Child:

function Child(props) {

  return (
    <button
      onClick={() => props.count++}
    >
      Increment
    </button>
  );
}


props.count++ attempts to mutate the received value. It does not correctly update the parent's React state.

Correct

Parent:

function Parent() {

  const [count, setCount] =
    useState(0);

  const increment = () => {
    setCount(count + 1);
  };

  return (
    <Child
      count={count}
      onIncrement={increment}
    />
  );
}


Child:

function Child(props) {

  return (
    <button
      onClick={props.onIncrement}
    >
      Increment
    </button>
  );
}


Flow:

Child DOES NOT update count directly.

Child
 ↓
onIncrement()
 ↓
Parent
 ↓
setCount()


