Mistake 3: Excessive Props Drilling

================================================================================

Props Drilling Example
function Grandparent() {

  const [data, setData] =
    useState('Hello');

  return (
    <Parent
      data={data}
      setData={setData}
    />
  );
}

function Parent(props) {

  return (
    <Child
      data={props.data}
      setData={props.setData}
    />
  );
}

function Child(props) {

  return (
    <h1>
      {props.data}
    </h1>
  );
}


Here Parent receives the values primarily to pass them to Child.

Context API - Advanced Alternative
import {
  createContext,
  useContext,
  useState
} from 'react';

const DataContext =
  createContext();

function Grandparent() {

  const [data, setData] =
    useState('Hello');

  return (
    <DataContext.Provider
      value={{
        data,
        setData
      }}
    >

      <Parent />

    </DataContext.Provider>
  );
}

function Child() {

  const { data } =
    useContext(DataContext);

  return (
    <h1>
      {data}
    </h1>
  );
}

Concept
Props Drilling

Grandparent
    ↓ props
Parent
    ↓ props
Child


Context

Provider
   ↓
Shared Context Value
   ↓
Consumer Component


Context is useful when data needs to be shared with components deeper in a tree and repeatedly forwarding props becomes undesirable.

