Mistake 4: Modifying State Directly

================================================================================

Wrong:

function Parent() {

  const [books, setBooks] =
    useState([...]);

  const addBook = (book) => {

    books.push(book);
  };

  return (
    <BookList books={books} />
  );
}


Correct:

function Parent() {

  const [books, setBooks] =
    useState([...]);

  const addBook = (book) => {

    setBooks([
      ...books,
      book
    ]);
  };

  return (
    <BookList books={books} />
  );
}

Difference
Direct Mutation           | State Setter
--------------------------|---------------------------------
books.push(book)          | setBooks([...books, book])
Mutates existing array    | Creates a new array
Doesn't use React setter  | Uses React state update mechanism
Avoid                     | Preferred


